          {
            title: 'LÃ³rum (Slovak)',
            subtitle: 'The Slovak Bidding Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "The Slovak version of LÃ³rum is a distinct trick-avoidance and bidding game, significantly different from its Hungarian namesake. Played with a 32-card German-suited deck, it focuses on 'Big' and 'Small' games where a single player often plays against a partnership of three. It is a game of high stakes and strict play rules, particularly the 'must-overtake' rule in the Small Game variant.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Part of the broader Central European family of 'LÃ³rum' and 'King' games, but evolved in the Slovak regions to emphasize solo bidding and 'Big/Small' contracts.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players. A dealer deals 8 cards to each player.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32 cards (standard Slovak deck). No permanent trumps.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck and counters.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '8 cards to each player.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
